      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've been experiencing this a bit, plus an issue with my legs not properly matching my height as well. When I stretch out my legs, my foot will keep going after my avatar's leg is already fully extended when previously this wasn't happening in other builds. I'm 5'9\" exactly and have to adjust my height by a few inches to have it be more accurate now. I'm not sure if it's just a strange issue for us because I haven't seen more comments about this, but it is something that I'm curious about.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-03T20:24:40.659Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The most recent update (VRChat 2022.2.1p4, build 1205) seems to have decreased the accuracy of heights, resulting in avatars appearing in the floor by an inch or two.\nPrior to this build, if I used my actual, real height (5'8\"), with the height measurement, my avatar would not be in the floor; my feet would be aligned perfectly with it.\nNow, however, my feet are in the floor by an inch or two; I have to set my height to 5'6\" to 5'7\" for it to be where it previously was.\nI'm  certain that 5'8\" is my real actual height. My placespace is also properly calibrated.\nAgain, this was a non-issue prior to the build that introduced walking animation toggling.",
